# <% .Name %>

The operator of the `<% .Group %>/<% .Kind %>` objects, built with the Norca
controller SDK. Scaffolded by `norca operator init`.

| File | |
| --- | --- |
| `<% .KindLower %>.kind.hcl`, `<% .KindLower %>.schema.json` | the object kind: JSON Schema with defaults, CEL rules, columns, version, webhook, limits |
| `examples/<% .KindLower %>.hcl` | a sample object |
| `types.go` | `Spec` and `Status` of the kind |
| `reconcile.go` | the reconciler: finalizer, status conditions, event log |
| `webhook.go` | the validating webhook (`<% .Name %> webhook`) |
| `main.go` | flags, API client, leader election, metrics |
| `reconcile_test.go` | tests against the SDK's fake backend |
| `envtest_test.go` | tests against a dev agent (needs the `norca` binary) |
| `pack/<% .Name %>` | the operator pack: kind, ACL policy, controller job |

## Develop

```shell
go mod tidy                     # after pointing the replace directives of go.mod at your Norca checkout
norca object-kind lint <% .KindLower %>.kind.hcl examples/<% .KindLower %>.hcl
go test ./...                   # fake backend; envtest_test.go also starts a dev agent if norca is on the PATH
```

Run the controller locally against a dev agent:

```shell
norca agent -dev &                               # in another terminal
norca object-kind apply <% .KindLower %>.kind.hcl
NORCA_ADDR=http://127.0.0.1:4646 go run . -leader-election=false
norca object apply examples/<% .KindLower %>.hcl
norca object list <% .Group %>/<% .Kind %>
norca object events <% .Group %>/<% .Kind %> sample
```

## Change the schema

Raise `version` in the kind and add a `migration` when stored objects would
no longer match the schema. `norca object-kind apply -dry-run` reports how
many objects change, which would be invalid, and sample conversions; the
servers reject a change that would make stored objects invalid.

## Install

```shell
go build -o /usr/local/bin/<% .Name %> .       # on every node, or build an image
norca pack run ./pack/<% .Name %> --name=<% .Name %>
```
